# Firebase Web API key in firebase-config.js — deliberately committed (see
# that file's own header comment and .gitignore's comment above it): the
# Firebase web API key is explicitly documented by Firebase itself as not a
# secret (https://firebase.google.com/docs/projects/api-keys), and this
# exact value is already downloaded to every visitor's browser as plain JS
# on the live production site regardless of whether it's in the repo. Real
# security here is Firebase Security Rules / Data Connect auth levels, not
# secrecy of this key.
